 3. 🐊 Florida&#x27;s Democratic Socialist surprise 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Angie Nixon high-fives Rep. Rashida Tlaib (D-Mich.) at a campaign rally in Fort Lauderdale last week. Photo: Dave Decker/ZUMA Press Wire via Reuters A stunning Florida Senate primary win by Angie Nixon (D) made her the first member of the Democratic Socialists of America to ever win a major-party nomination for statewide office, Axios' Andrew Pantazi, Marc Caputo and Holly Otterbein write. 

 Nixon beat former Trump impeachment witness Alex Vindman in a major upset ( 56.1% to 43.9% ). Nixon faces an extreme uphill battle against incumbent Republican Sen. Ashley Moody, who's heavily favored . 🌴 More Florida results: In an open contest to replace term-limited Gov. Ron DeSantis, Rep. Byron Donalds won the Republican nomination.

 Scandal-plagued Rep. Cory Mills (R-Fla.) lost his primary to former TV reporter Ryan Elijah (34.1% to 47.3%) . Rep. Debbie Wasserman Schultz (D) won her primary (45.3%) in a historically Black-represented district after her district was eliminated, but the majority of the vote split among four Black challengers. Keep reading . 

 
 
