 6. 🪖 Trump&#x27;s 6 months of war 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Photo illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios. Photos: Joaquin Sarmiento/AFP and Aaron Schwartz/CNP/Bloomberg via Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The Iran war will hit the half-year mark next week (Aug. 28), with Washington and Tehran each betting it can outlast the other, Axios Future of Defense author Colin Demarest writes. 

 Why it matters: The war's length is pushing once-niche national-security issues — munitions levels , defense contracting, at-sea replenishment — into everyday conversation. 🌐 Trump said this week he wants to claim the Strait of Hormuz and posted a map on Truth Social labeling it a "U.S. territory."

